From: TDVP Device Team <devices@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] oggdemux: retain initial push segment sequence number

An upstream muxer can deliver a TIME segment. The BYTES seek path is
unchanged; retain the initial upstream sequence number in the other path
so subsequently generated segment/EOS events do not receive INVALID.

--- a/ext/ogg/gstoggdemux.c
+++ b/ext/ogg/gstoggdemux.c
@@ -2534,6 +2534,12 @@
           GST_PUSH_UNLOCK (ogg);
         } else {
+          /* A push-mode muxer may supply a TIME segment. Preserve its
+           * sequence number without changing the BYTES seeking path. */
+          GST_PUSH_LOCK (ogg);
+          if (ogg->seqnum == GST_SEQNUM_INVALID)
+            ogg->seqnum = gst_event_get_seqnum (event);
+          GST_PUSH_UNLOCK (ogg);
           GST_WARNING_OBJECT (ogg, "unexpected segment format: %s",
               gst_format_get_name (segment.format));
         }
       }
